 "note": "Busselton Bowling Club, Brown St, from the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026). A long single-storey clubhouse on the north side of its four greens: a big hipped hall under a pale green Colorbond roof (solar panels on the north slope), a lower hipped west wing, flat-roofed kitchen and store rooms at the east end, and a white flat verandah along the whole front looking over the two main greens. Green-roofed seating shelters stand along the south edge of the greens, backed onto the street, with a low wire fence along the boundary. The greens themselves are ground (the base's aerial). Front = the greens side (south-south-east), which is what drivers on the street see across the greens. Metres: x west to east along the greens, y north from the verandah edge.",
